Backport of "Avoid state corruption via bailout" to PHP 5.6.40 (EOL, no official backport).

Fix GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w (CVE-2026-109618) -- OOM/alloc-overflow longjmp state corruption
Fix GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp (CVE-2026-109619) -- stale request-owned global state reuse

UNOFFICIAL analogy backport. PHP 5.6 uses the OLD Zend engine (old zend_mm allocator,
old HashTable with Bucket **arBuckets, no zend_string, TSRMLS_* thread macros), so this
is NOT a direct application of the official 7.4 diff (upstream commit
712e60f9edfd03f0960fc4fc3c2c375f42b90aa2); the defensive intent is identical, the code is
adapted to 5.x idioms. zend_mm_safe_error_ex() is exported ZEND_API so the Zend/zend_strtod.c
Balloc() OOM site can also be redirected off the longjmp path (parity with the 5.4 sibling).
See port-notes/56.md for every mapped/adapted/N-A item and reasons.

Apply from the pristine php-5.6.40 tree root with:
    patch -p1 --forward --batch < php-5.6.patch

